From: AssassinK786 <85348050+AssassinK786@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:04:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] 7-series: 3D Skyline, a build's FASM drawn on its die
 (the FASM skyline widget of the umbrella checkout)

- 3D Skyline (process under Place & Route, POST/GET /projects/:p/skyline, MCP fpga_skyline; server/skyline.js, web/js/skyline.js): the open build's nextpnr FASM, or Vivado's bitstream decoded by bit2fasm (Cross-Check's FASM when as new as the routed design); never a FASM older than the build.
- The die's grid from Project X-Ray's tilegrid.json and the page made by the widget's own scripts (paths.skyline, else <silinx>/../skyline, served as /vendor/skyline/); the interface's page loads them from there, its constants in a JSON element (the pages' Content-Security-Policy runs no inline script); build/skyline.html offline.
- fpga_skyline: the page's counts (features, tiles, tallest tile, families, tallest columns); Portuguese label; tests (skyline, the tool lists, the routes); changelog fragment (its issue number a placeholder, 9000).
